      },
      {
        "line": 84,
        "text": "- `--no_net_names`                    Omits net names in the extracted netlist."
      },
      {
        "line": 85,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 86,
        "text": "- `--spice_comments`                  Includes netlist comments in the extracted netlist."
      },
      {
        "line": 87,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 88,
        "text": "- `--net_only`                        Generates netlist objects only in the extracted netlist."
      },
      {
        "line": 89,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 96,
        "text": "- `--combine_devices`                 Enables device combination for both layout and schematic netlists."
      },
      {
        "line": 97,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 98,
        "text": "- `--disable_tap_extraction`          Skips `ntap1`/`ptap1` device extraction so taps are not required in the schematic, matching Magic+Netgen LVS behavior. Extraction is enabled by default."
      },
      {
        "line": 99,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 100,
        "text": "- `--top_lvl_pins`                    Creates pins for top-level circuits in both layout and schematic netlists."
      },
      {
        "line": 101,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 102,
        "text": "- `--purge`                           Removes unused nets from both layout and schematic netlists."
      },
      {
        "line": 103,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 104,
        "text": "- `--purge_nets`                      Purges floating nets from both layout and schematic netlists."
      },
      {
        "line": 105,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 106,
        "text": "- `--ignore_top_ports_mismatch`       Ignores top-level port mismatches during comparison mode."
      },
      {
        "line": 107,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 108,
        "text": "- `--implicit_nets=<nets>`            Comma-separated net names/patterns for implicit connections (case-sensitive), e.g., `\"VDD,VSS\"` or `\"*\"`."
      },
      {
        "line": 109,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 148,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 149,
        "text": "```bash"
      },
      {
        "line": 150,
        "text": "    python3 run_lvs.py --layout=testing/testcases/unit/mos_devices/layout/sg13_lv_nmos.gds --netlist=testing/testcases/unit/mos_devices/netlist/sg13_lv_nmos.cdl --run_dir=test_nmos --ignore_top_ports_mismatch --implicit_nets=VDD,VSS"
      },
      {
        "line": 151,
        "text": "```"
      },
      {
        "line": 152,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 153,
        "text": "#### LVS Outputs"
      },
      {
        "line": 154,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 155,
        "text": "You could find the run results at your run directory if you previously specified it through `--run_dir=<run_dir_path>`. Default path of run directory is `lvs_run_<date>_<time>` in current directory."
      },
      {
        "line": 156,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 157,
        "text": "**Folder Structure of run results**"
      },
      {
        "line": 158,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 159,
        "text": "```text"
      },
      {
        "line": 160,
        "text": "\ud83d\udcc1 lvs_run_<date>_<time>"
      },
      {
        "line": 161,
        "text": " \u2523 \ud83d\udcdc lvs_run_<date>_<time>.log"
      },
      {
        "line": 197,
        "text": "</p>"
      },
      {
        "line": 198,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 199,
        "text": "Additionally, you can find the extracted netlist generated from your design at (`<device_name>_extracted.cir`) in the output run directory."
      },
      {
        "line": 200,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 201,
        "text": "At the end of each CLI run, `run_lvs.py` prints an **Important Summary** table that highlights:"
      },
      {
        "line": 202,
        "text": "- run status and mode"
      },
      {
        "line": 203,
        "text": "- final LVS outcome"
      },
      {
        "line": 204,
        "text": "- results directory path"
      },
      {
        "line": 205,
        "text": "- warning/error counts and key messages"
      },
      {
        "line": 206,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 207,
        "text": "### GUI"
      },
      {
        "line": 208,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 209,
        "text": "The SG13G2 also facilitates LVS execution via Klayout menus as depicted below:"
      },
      {
        "line": 210,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 261,
        "text": "</p>"
      },
      {
        "line": 262,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 263,
        "text": "Upon executing the LVS, a live log window is shown and the generated result database is loaded on your layout interface automatically, allowing you to verify the outcome as shown above in Fig. 4."
      },
      {
        "line": 264,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 265,
        "text": "Additionally, all run outputs (log, extracted netlist, report database) are available in the selected `Output Run Directory`."
      }
    ]
